---
// Starlight's ThemeProvider, replaced so the docs follow the same rule as the
// rest of the site rather than their own: light is the default, dark only where
// the visitor asked for it. This reads the same versioned key the marketing
// pages write, so a choice made in the navbar carries into the docs and back.
//
// It used to hard-pin dark, with a comment saying that matched the marketing
// site. That stopped being true when light became the default there.
//
// The attribute is always written, never deleted. Starlight server-renders
// data-theme="dark" and both its stylesheet and the Expressive Code one key
// their light values off data-theme="light", so an absent attribute leaves the
// docs dark. Our own tokens match on :not([data-theme="dark"]), so an explicit
// "light" satisfies both.
---
<script is:inline>
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme =
        localStorage.getItem("kyde_theme_choice") === "dark" ? "dark" : "light";
</script>
